{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162825-mind-control-and-spheres","id":1162825,"title":"Mind control and spheres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-26T16:48:01-08:00","id":1162825,"title":"Mind control and spheres","content":"So... What happens if one mafe uses a Mind 4 effect to take full control of another mage and tries to use magic in that body? Could he use only the spheres he knows and the mage he is currently controling too? Can he use any sphere he knows regarldless the other mage not knowing them? Would this just simply not work? If it does work, would it be with a penalty? There is one penalty for &quot;In conflict with your Avatar&quot; so I assume this kinda applies to this case. And what happens if you cast Vulgar magic with witnesses? Would the Paradox go to your original body or to the body you are currently possessing?<br /> <br /> Is it possible to do a total mind transfer permanently? For cases where you want to cheat death by just bodysurfing to a younger body. If that is the case, what would happen to the other mage mind? Would you have to erase his mind entirely? Could it be possible to resurface from time to time and start to fight for control?<br /> <br /> Mind Sphere kind of seems OP if you take this into account.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T19:20:15-08:00","id":1162863,"title":"","content":"Interesting question. The conclusion I come to, oddly enough, is that with <i>complete</i> control, full puppetry, you wouldn't be able to control their magic. The Avatar after all is separate from the mind. But with less complete control--suggestions all the way up to series of commands--you can use Mind to compel a mage to use their magic to serve your will. Magic requires some measure of will from someone attached to a specific Avatar. Magic should become more challenging the less a mage is in control of his own mind. Having one's emotions moderately influenced would incur no penalty; a long string of commands that go against a mage's Nature and better interest might mean a +2 or +3 difficulty on Arete rolls.<br /> <br /> If you were possessing someone's body you could use your own Spheres, just like you can when using Mind to astral project. In the longer term it raises questions. So their mind is taken over, what about their soul, and their Avatar (if it is not the same as the soul)? Over time I would think it would slowly bring the invading mind in line with its Nature or give it a dual Nature. Same with the Essence. A powerful enough soul might even be able to eject the invader. For assurance of permanent body snatching you should probably also have Spirit 5.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T23:37:33-08:00","id":1162917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrakeEpsilon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162825-mind-control-and-spheres#post1162825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... What happens if one mafe uses a Mind 4 effect to take full control of another mage</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that it's possible to take full control of a True Mage with Mind 4. Where did you read anything that made you think it is possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T04:11:31-08:00","id":1162951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162825-mind-control-and-spheres?p=1162917#post1162917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that it's possible to take full control of a True Mage with Mind 4. Where did you read anything that made you think it is possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind 4 is ALL ABOUT mind control and possession. That and astral projection.<br /> <br /> Course, it matters how we define the phrase &quot;take full control&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think a mage can use another mage's Awakened ability, even with mind control. They can order the mage to cast their own Effects - assuming it doesn't countermand the controlled mage's Awakened Will - but possessing the target or mind controlling them won't let you freely use their power. Even if you are in their body, and try to cast a spell, you're just casting spells YOU are able to cast using someone else's body. Which, depending on your Focus, might not work. Both a cyborg and an Akashic martial artist would see their Arts as an extension of their bodies, with all the work they've put into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T04:17:35-08:00","id":1162953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162825-mind-control-and-spheres?p=1162951#post1162951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 4 is ALL ABOUT mind control and possession. That and astral projection.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It can also be used to make somebody have a very strong impression about another person or an event, for example. I would say this is definitely not the same as what you're calling 'mind control'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T04:53:54-08:00","id":1162956,"title":"","content":"While Mind 4 is enough to do mind control, the issue isn't the sphere level its that under the current rules its exceedingly difficult for any mage to mind control another mage or nightfolk. Per the M20 rules the difficulty to use the Mind sphere on a mage (or other nightfolk) is their Willpower + 3 (pg 519 of M20).<br /> <br /> That means the minimum difficulty to mess with a fellow mage's mind is 8 if their Willpower is only 5 to as high as difficulty 13 (so difficulty 9 or 10 with a significant threshold) if they've got Willpower 10. If the target has even one dot in Mind themselves they can make a coincidental Arete roll at base difficulty 4 to counter any successes you do score (they would also be able to sense the use of Mind magic against them and so would get to make a difficulty 6 Willpower roll to cancel even more successes... which unaware targets do not get).<br /> <br /> <i>How Do You Do That? (pg 123)</i> further establishes that to force someone to do something they don't want to do you would need to score successes equal to the target's Willpower to make them comply. If you want to take total command of a target you need to score either 10 successes or successes equal to twice their Willpower, whichever is higher or the effect fails. Then you have to add duration to it.<br /> <br /> So you MIGHT be able to gain control of a low willpower mage who doesn't know the Mind sphere with an extended ritual (difficulty 8; 10 successes needed), but good luck targeting one with Willpower 8 (difficulty 11; 16 successes needed), much less Willpower 10 (difficulty 13; 20 successes needed) and those odds drop like a stone if they have even one dot in Mind themselves (Arete 1, Willpower 5 would cancel about 3.4 successes with just a reflexive defense on average... while Arete 3, Willpower 10 would cancel 6.3 successes).<br /> <br /> You'd be much better off mind-controlling one of the target mage's Sleeper loved ones (2-4 willpower means base difficulty is only 4 +3 if you want to be able to force them to take suicidal actions; with 10 successes needed for complete control) and then blackmailing the mage to do what you want them to do. That way their magic use isn't compromised either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}